      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay [zone=1059]\n**Who:**\n- Mayor Soltiman Wex [ _Mayor and Quest Giver_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Time:** | 6 Hours\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 00:03:00\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Carmit Ellison [npc=50437]\n- a persuaded citizen [npc=50390]\n**Era:** | !The Broken Mirror\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Dec 3 00:51:48 2015\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | 6 hour task timer. 3 hour lockout. This a shared task that is the third task given Mayor Soltiman Wex.\nTo get the task say, 'black and white'\nShort Version\nTask Progression\nSpeak with Carmit Ellison 0/1 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nFound wandering in the north eastern part of the zone. Hail update.\nChange persuaded citizen' minds 0/5 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nSay wrong and see if it attacks.\nKill persuaded citzens 0/5 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nSay 'wrong' and kill it if it attacks.\nReturn to Mayor Soltiman Wex 0/1 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nHail update.\nReward(s):\n150 platinum\nYou gain experience!! (2 AA)\n333 Remnants of Tranquility\n\n---\n\nLong version\nYou say, 'black and white'\nMayor Soltiman Wex says 'I am a bit... concerned... by a recalcitrant priest that goes by the name of Carmit Ellison. He is speaking out publicly against pursuing eternal life in the service of Anashti Sul. This priest has persuaded many citizens to rethink following the goddess. He has a right to speak his mind in Sul Vius, and it would not be proper to harm him, but there are other ways to reverse the damage he's done.'\nMayor Soltiman Wex is concerned that a recalcitrant priest is speaking out publicly against pursuing eternal life in the service of Anashti Sul. She has persuaded many citizens to rethink following the goddess. She has a right to pseak her mind in Sul Vius, and it woudl not do to harm her, but there are ways to reverse the damage she's done.\nFind the preacher, Carmit Ellison, in the heights. Speak with her.\nTask Progression\nSpeak with Carmit Ellison 0/1 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nFound wandering in the north eastern part of the zone. Hail update.\nYou say, 'Hail, Carmit Ellison'\nCarmit Ellison says 'Bad news, friend. The endless life that Anashti and her followers are peddling is a dead end. I have seen the transitions. I have walked them myself, from beginning, to middle, to the end. This pursuit merely led to a hollow existence. It was not peace, but emptiness. Certainly, you can live forever by accepting Anashti Sul's gifts, but what's the value of a future that involves sacrificing every shred of your individuality only to be shackled in servitude? Anashti Sul is a second-rate goddess that should have remained forgotten. Ask around. I've been speaking to the citizens here and they now see the real truth.'\nChange persuaded citizen' minds 0/5 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nThe persuaded citizens are in the northeast area.\nSay wrong and see if it attacks.\nYou say, 'Hail, a persuaded citizen'\na persuaded citizen is startled, 'Oh, you startled me. I was just thinking about what the preacher was saying. Perhaps the eternal life the goddess is offering isn't what I want. Am I [wrong] to think that?'\nYou say, 'Wrong'\na persuaded citizen muses, 'You're right. I shouldn't be so quick to give up my pursuit of eternal life in the service of Anashti Sul. There are many tests of one's faith, and I think I can overcome this one. Thank you.'\nKill persuaded citzens 0/5 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nSay 'wrong' and kill it if it attacks.\nYou say, 'Hail, a persuaded citizen'\na persuaded citizen is startled, 'Oh, you startled me. I was just thinking about what the preacher was saying. Perhaps the eternal life the goddess is offering isn't what I want. Am I [wrong] to think that?'\nYou say, 'Wrong'\na persuaded citizen says 'You're just a puppet of Anashti Sul! Ellison was right about everything!'\nReturn to Mayor Soltiman Wex 0/1 (Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay)\nHail update.\nYou say, 'Hail, Mayor Soltiman Wex'\nMayor Soltiman Wex licks a festering sore on his lip, thoughtfully, 'That's what happens when you disrupt the order in my city. Someone gets hurt. Now that you've set things straight, I have a [personal favor] to ask.'\nReward(s):\n150 platinum\nYou gain experience!! (2 AA)\n333 Remnants of Tranquility\n**Submitted by:** Tarvas\n- Remnant of Tranquility [item=124218]",
