      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sul Vius: Demiplane of Life [zone=1058]\n**Who:**\n- Anna Broth [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Anna Broth's Recruitment Poster [item=124196]\n- Shard of Healing [item=124646]\n- Stolen Life Fragment [item=124872]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Sul Vius: Demiplane of Decay [zone=1059]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Fenlu Coi [npc=50227]\n**Era:** | !The Broken Mirror\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Wed Jun 8 00:33:49 2016\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | Turn in Anna Broth's Recruitment Poster [item=124196] to Anna Broth [npc=50264]. You get these from clicking on books in Demiplane of Decay. One was given when you clicked on books in \"Familiar Haunts\" The poster is returned after you get the task and only one person in the group needs to turn in the poster.\nAnna Broth looks at the poster and sighs, smiling weakly. 'That was a good day.'\nTravel to the Plane of Health.\nZone into Plane of Health for update.\nSpeak with Fenlu Coi.\nHead to the northern most circular structure in the middle ring area. Drop invis and hail Fenlu for update.\nFenlu Coi listens to your story and looks genuinely concerned, 'You were right to bring this to me. This is troubling news, both of your friends and of Anashti Sul's plane. I will help you rescue your friends as best as I can, and I believe you can [help] me too.'\nFenlu Coi gestures behind her and says, 'Anashti's plane is not the only one with decay problems. Bertoxxulous' minions have been [invading] this area as well, stealing fragments of life.'\nFenlu Coi says, 'Puslings, bubonians, and the whole lot of Bertoxxulous' atrocities have been creeping through tombs into this plane to steal pieces of Rodcet's power. We'll need a few of those to heal your friends. Open rifts at the tombs in this area, and kill whatever comes through to get stolen life fragments. Once you have enough, bring them to me.'\nThe next three stages open up together. You must click on one of the three graves to initiate several waves of mobs. The mobs all spawn on top of the grave, do not immediately agro, and are all significantly easier than normal trash. Once all waves are dead, the rift closes. Repeat for all 3 - these are located at (2580, 430, -37), (2730, 360, -31), (2750, 100, -40). All mobs are rootable and snarable. The waves of a single mob drop 3x Stolen Life Fragments.\nWave 1: 3x low HP trash - either 3x a bloody bubonian or 3x a foul pulsing\nWave 2: 1x a bubonian mystic - humanoid\nWave 3: 1x a pestilence priest and 2x low HP trash - mix comprising of a bloody bubonian, a foul pulsing, or a corrupted pulsing\nWave 4: 1x a Banord underling or 1x a Rutyl knight\nSeal invasion rift. 0/3\nClick on tombs which are around the circular structure that Fenlu is located in. Task will not update until all mobs coming out of tomb are dead\nKill underlings decay invaders 0/15\nEach tomb gave me 4 waves. Usually multiple (2 or 3), then a single, then multiple (2 or 3), then single. They were easy kills, all dark blue to lvl 105. I got NO XP for killing these mobs.\nLoot Stolen Life Fragments 0/10.\nThey are on corpses, usually 2-3 per corpse. Got all of mine by second tomb.\nThe Shard of Healing is a powerful artifact of healing. If you lose it, Fenlu can give you another one.\nGive stolen Life Fragments to Fenlu.\nTurn in Life Fragments to Fenlu. Each person in task will get a \"Shard of healing\" in their bags\nTravel to Demiplane of Decay.\nHead back to Demiplane of Life and then use Mirror fragment to zone into Demiplane of Decay.\nThe next three stages open up together. You must right click the Shard of Healing on the targeted mobs when their health is under 50%. You will frequently need to use your mirror to phase to the Plane of Decay and Life to navigate and complete these stages.\nAbsorb Resurrected Corpses 0/5 Demiplane of Decay.\nYou can't get to the graveyard in Demiplane of Decay by just running into the graveyard area. You need go to the merchant area (east) and use the trap door in the plaza (where all the merchant's booths are). You will come out in the large building in the center of the zone. Go south to the graves and 1st one there will spawn the resurrected corpse. 1 at a time will spawn, get on the south wall and fight them to 50% and then use your Shard of Healing to absorb them for update.\nYou must be in Decay for this step. A safe place to phase is behind a tree by the wall at -1000, -320, 40. Walk to one of the piles graves to spawn a resurrected corpse. Beat it to under 50% and click your shard. Each grave has a cool-down period of several minutes before it can be used again, or you can move to another grave.\nA resurrected corpse rises out of a nearby grave, drawn to the Shard of Healing you carry.\nA resurrected corpse is weakened. Use the Shard of Healing now to absorb its essence!\nYour Shard of Healing begins to glow.\nThe creature dissolves as its life essence is absorbed into the Shard of Healing.\nAbsorb Weakened Sentinels 0/3 Demiplane of Decay.\nLeave the graveyard area by going back through the tunnel but this time turn left at the junction and head to the long hallway with all the rooms off it. Sentinels are in the long hallway. Fight them to 50% and then use your Shard of Healing to absorb them for updates. I went to the center of the room, absorbed the 1 roamer that went back and forth between the two entrances and then fought the 2 at the end of the hall.\nThe sentinels con indifferent without any invis, but are social. They are pacifiable, snare and rootable. A safe place to phase to Decay is -610, -77, -100. the sentinels are slightly tougher than the zombies, hitting up to 15k.\nA venerated sentinel says, 'An intruder in our city. It must be dealt with.\nAbsorb Silent Devotees 0/5 Demiplane of Life.\nHead back to Demiplane of Life. Go to the merchant area and stand next to a merchant's booth. Silent devotees will spawn and run to you. You just have to use your Shard of Healing on the devotees and absorb them to update your task.\nThe silent devotees are on the Life side. They spawn in the area to the east of the graveyard around -420, -420, 10. Their mechanic seems to be broken as they spawn at 10% health, charge you, but are non-agro. Simply keep targeting and clicking your shard without fighting anything.\nFocus Shard of Healing on the apparitions.\nHead back to Anna Broth and absorb an apparition in a cage by her for an update.\nAbsorb Lonyen.\nStay near Anna Broth and switch over to Demiplane of Decay. Absorb Lonyen for update.\n-350, -120, -25 is a safe place to phase into Decay. Hug the wall NW of Lonyen and you can click your shard on him without getting aggro.\nSpeak with Anna Broth.\nGo back to Demiplane of Life and hail Anna for update.\nFind the underground bar's back room.\nHead to the central pit and go down 1 level and into the building. Go into the room in the far right corner for task update.\nThe trigger for this is at -400, -15, -110. This is the first set of rooms down the ramp form the zone in. the back room is the farthest west room with a see-invis (but too short to see over the bar) barman.\nUse the Shard of Healing to preserve the adventures' essence.\nUse your Shard of Healing on any person in the room to complete the task.\nMultiple non-agro mobs appear to the NW corner of the room, jumping for a glowing blue shard. Avoid the temptation to click this shard as doing so causes them to despawn, invis to drop and the room to agro. It does not impact the mission in any way.\nReward(s):\nXP\n225pp\n500 Remnants of Tranquility\n**Submitted by:** Hakir\n- Remnant of Tranquility [item=124218]",
